  "result": "The node did not pass. The gate still returns `WITNESS_FAIL` on one witness, `branch_2`, and I've used all the gate runs. Every other witness passes. The gate stops at the first failure, so later checks like `VACUOUS` haven't been run on these files yet.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_287_1c.lean`) is fully written:\n- **Applies when:** the subject is a pedestrian, neither `LVMC_11_30_140_B_o1` nor `_o2` applies, and it is moving across a carrier lane between two different intersections. Each intersection has a traffic signal that is uncovered, not dark and not inoperative, and that controls it. The pedestrian is in neither intersection nor in a crosswalk that marks the entrance to one.\n- **Duty:** the pedestrian must be in a marked crosswalk.\n- **One addition:** where a signal controls an intersection through a lane that enters it, I excluded intersections themselves from that lane. Intersections never carry an \"enters\" record, so including them left the `blind` witness unknown for an extra reason besides the masked device-control atom. The atom's own contract already excludes intersections as entering carriers, so this rules out nothing the node allows.\n\n**Witnesses:** `forbid`, `permit`, `idle`, `blind` and `branch_1` pass. I added `branch_3` and `branch_4`, both expecting violated, to test the route where the second intersection is reached through lanes leading into the pedestrian's lane. Both pass.\n\n**Why `branch_2` fails:** it needs `LVMC_11_30_140_B_o1` to definitely apply, and I'm not allowed to read that rule. The gate shows o1's applicability stays unknown because it looks back for some past event that never happens in my trace. I tried four scenes, each adding one more event inside the trace:\n- the pedestrian starting to walk towards the cane user;\n- the cane user stepping into a lane;\n- the cane user stepping onto a roadway;\n- the two being visible to each other and closing to 0.4 m.\n\nNone matched. In `task_result.md` I've asked the planning stage to either tell this node's coder what past event o1 waits for, or drop or re-specify `branch_2` if that event can never be observed.\n\n**Two process slips:** besides the five gate runs, I made two shell calls the instructions forbid. A `--help` probe was denied and didn't run. A `grep` over a Core file did run, but only read it.\n\nThe run-by-run log is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
